# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers, or under Git Bash on Windows.
# Both break on CRLF — a container entrypoint with \r fails to exec at all,
# and bash reports `$'\r': command not found`. A Windows customer cloning
# with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise get exactly that on first run, so
# these files are pinned to LF regardless of anyone's git settings.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the other way round.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Let git decide for everything else.
*               text=auto
